## 3. The Build Contract (v1)

### 3.1 Inputs (environment variables)

| Variable | Required | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `IMAGE_NAME` | yes | — | Full image repo, e.g. `registry.company.com/team/app`. No tag. |
| `IMAGE_TAGS` | no | `$CI_COMMIT_SHA` | Space-separated tags, e.g. `"1.4.0 latest"`. |
| `DOCKERFILE` | no | `Dockerfile` | Path relative to context. |
| `BUILD_CONTEXT` | no | `.` | Build context directory. |
| `BUILD_ARGS` | no | empty | Space-separated `KEY=VALUE` pairs. |
| `BUILD_SECRETS` | no | empty | Space-separated `id=path` pairs, mounted as build secrets (never baked into layers). |
| `PLATFORMS` | no | `linux/amd64` | Comma-separated, e.g. `linux/amd64,linux/arm64`. |
| `CACHE_REF` | no | `$IMAGE_NAME:buildcache` | Registry ref used for layer cache. |
| `PUSH` | no | `true` | `false` = build only (PR validation builds). |
| `LABELS` | no | empty | Space-separated `KEY=VALUE` OCI labels. |
| `TARGET` | no | empty | Multi-stage build target stage. |

### 3.2 Outputs

| Artifact | Description |
|---|---|
| Pushed image(s) | `$IMAGE_NAME:<tag>` for every tag in `IMAGE_TAGS` (when `PUSH=true`). |
| `image.digest` | File in the job workspace containing the image digest (`sha256:...`). Downstream jobs (deploy, sign, scan) consume this — never re-resolve tags. |
| `image.ref` | File containing the full pinned reference `IMAGE_NAME@sha256:...`. |

### 3.3 Guarantees

- Output is a standard OCI image, pullable by any runtime.
- Registry-based layer caching across ephemeral runners (Kaniko `--cache-repo` equivalent).
- Build secrets never persist in image layers.
- Exit code non-zero on any failure; partial pushes are not treated as success.

### 3.4 Explicit non-goals

- No passthrough of raw builder flags.
- No promise about *how* the image is built (daemon, rootless, remote builder). Pipelines must not assume a Docker socket exists.

