## 5. Repository 2: `platform/ci-templates`

### 5.1 `templates/build-image.yml`

```yaml
# Org-standard image build job. App pipelines extend this and set variables.
# Contract docs: platform/image-builder/README.md

.build-image:
  image: registry.company.com/platform/image-builder:1   # pinned MAJOR
  variables:
    # remote rootless buildkitd (Kubernetes runners), see infra docs §7
    BUILDKIT_ADDR: "tcp://buildkitd.ci-build.svc.cluster.local:1234"
  before_script:
    # registry auth — the one infra concern handled here, not in app repos
    - mkdir -p ~/.docker
    - >
      echo "{\"auths\":{\"$CI_REGISTRY\":{\"auth\":\"$(printf '%s:%s' "$CI_REGISTRY_USER" "$CI_REGISTRY_PASSWORD" | base64 -w0)\"}}}"
      > ~/.docker/config.json
  script:
    - build-image.sh
  artifacts:
    paths: [image.digest, image.ref]
    expire_in: 1 week
```

Pin the template repo itself with a `ref:` when including (next section), so template changes also roll out deliberately.

### 5.2 What an application pipeline looks like

```yaml
include:
  - project: platform/ci-templates
    ref: v1                       # pinned template version
    file: templates/build-image.yml

build:
  extends: .build-image
  stage: build
  variables:
    IMAGE_NAME: $CI_REGISTRY_IMAGE
    IMAGE_TAGS: "$CI_COMMIT_SHA latest"
    BUILD_ARGS: "APP_VERSION=$CI_COMMIT_SHA"

# downstream example — consumes the contract output, never the tool
deploy:
  stage: deploy
  needs: [build]
  script:
    - IMAGE_REF=$(cat image.ref)
    - helm upgrade myapp ./chart --set image.ref=$IMAGE_REF
```

**This is the entire surface area an app team ever sees.** No buildx, no Kaniko, no daemon details.

