## 8. Contract Tests (the safety net for future swaps)

`tests/contract-test.sh` runs in the `image-builder` repo's own pipeline on every MR:

```bash
#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail
TEST_IMAGE="${CI_REGISTRY_IMAGE}/contract-test"

# 1. basic build + push produces digest outputs
IMAGE_NAME=$TEST_IMAGE IMAGE_TAGS=$CI_COMMIT_SHA \
  BUILD_CONTEXT=tests/sample-app build-image.sh
test -s image.digest && grep -q '^sha256:' image.digest
test -s image.ref

# 2. image is pullable by digest
crane manifest "$(cat image.ref)" >/dev/null

# 3. build args are applied
IMAGE_NAME=$TEST_IMAGE IMAGE_TAGS=args-$CI_COMMIT_SHA \
  BUILD_ARGS="GREETING=hello" BUILD_CONTEXT=tests/sample-app build-image.sh
crane config "$TEST_IMAGE:args-$CI_COMMIT_SHA" | jq -e '.config.Env | index("GREETING=hello")'

# 4. second build hits cache (heuristic: completes much faster / logs CACHED)
start=$(date +%s)
IMAGE_NAME=$TEST_IMAGE IMAGE_TAGS=cache-$CI_COMMIT_SHA \
  BUILD_CONTEXT=tests/sample-app build-image.sh
echo "cached build took $(( $(date +%s) - start ))s"

# 5. PUSH=false does not push
PUSH=false IMAGE_NAME=$TEST_IMAGE IMAGE_TAGS=nopush \
  BUILD_CONTEXT=tests/sample-app build-image.sh
! crane manifest "$TEST_IMAGE:nopush" >/dev/null 2>&1

echo "contract v1: ALL TESTS PASSED"
```

When you swap the backend in the future: green contract tests on the new implementation = consumers are safe.

