## Appendix A: Other CI systems (same contract)

**GitHub Actions** — wrap as a composite action in a central repo:

```yaml
# org/.github/actions/build-image/action.yml
runs:
  using: docker
  image: docker://registry.company.com/platform/image-builder:1
```

**Jenkins** — shared library step:

```groovy
def call(Map cfg) {
  docker.image('registry.company.com/platform/image-builder:1').inside {
    withEnv(["IMAGE_NAME=${cfg.imageName}", "IMAGE_TAGS=${cfg.tags ?: env.GIT_COMMIT}"]) {
      sh 'build-image.sh'
    }
  }
}
// usage in Jenkinsfile:  buildImage(imageName: 'registry.company.com/team/app')
```

The builder image and contract are shared across all CI systems; only the thin template layer is per-system.
